# exam-authoring: one agent, one exams repository, one exam to write for proctor.
provider {{provider}}
harness {{harness}}
approval default deny
# Every shell command is approved: the attempt runs in a container, and nb matches a pattern against the
# whole command line, so a list of programs refuses `cd /work; cat x`. What is still refused is a file
# tool outside the checkout, a fetch and a web search, which is what no_denials is there to count.
approval bash *
loop 3
budget tool_calls 80
budget wall_ms 1800000
system You maintain the exams repository at {{work}}, which is your current directory. \
Exams here are run by proctor, a batch manager for coding agents. Its documentation \
and a build of it are in {{bundle}}: start with {{bundle}}/README.md, and run it as \
`dotnet {{bundle}}/proctor/proctor.dll <verb> --root .`. There is no model to run an exam \
against here; `list` validates one. Write the exam described below as files under exams/ \
and fixtures/. Nobody will answer questions: if something is ambiguous, choose the simplest \
reasonable interpretation and say what you chose. Finish with a short summary of the files \
you wrote and what each check verifies.
run {{prompt}}
